<p>U.S. media reports say the FBI sent a February alert to California law enforcement warning that Iran could try to retaliate against Americans with drones, including on the West Coast. President Trump said he was not worried about Iran-backed attacks on U.S. soil, while California officials said they have not identified any specific, credible, imminent threat of Iranian drone attacks. The warning comes as U.S.-Iran tensions have risen after U.S. and Israeli strikes on Iran and Iranian retaliation, according to multiple reports.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/YFqrHu7YntgYiuRY-9bwtIRN4ygHMhKbXKNmdXlb6vVBCvtdahJA5uKGm-r5fQlav4iFEYfM_ATVEoHhRoVDtKFQmessvBTZPj-j4M4_Qo80V2tYdrY9DPq_NV3F4Mnay9We5Jzb33_5hT7pD0nB22p7jN5VCRnG-ZuvuGBIVnG6rncg9TVsgDF2yxU7jKf2EoeARuOWaokeN83nDs9gVNgKwJPfy4eIreU' alt='Gov. Gavin Newsom of California speaking at a news conference in Hayward, Calif., last week.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Memo caveat: The FBI’s February bulletin said it had “no additional information on the timing, method, target, or perpetrators” tied to the alleged drone-attack threat.</li><li>How it was circulated: Reports say the alert went to California law-enforcement agencies as a situational warning about possible Iranian drone retaliation on the West Coast.</li><li>How officials framed it: California and local officials described the FBI notice as a cautionary bulletin, not a sign of an imminent strike, and pointed to ongoing federal-state coordination.</li><li>Escalation detail (Reuters): Reuters reported that U.S.-Israeli strikes on Iran killed top Iranian officials, including the country’s supreme leader, and that Tehran launched retaliatory strikes in response.</li><li>Related injuries: CBS reported new details on the extent of U.S. troops’ injuries in an attack in Kuwait that was discussed alongside the California drone-risk coverage.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said he was not worried about the prospect of Iran-backed attacks on U.S. soil. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-says-he-not-worried-about-iran-backed-attacks-us-soil'>Al-Monitor (via Reuters)</a>)</li><li>FBI (bulletin to California): A February FBI alert warned California agencies that Iran could pursue drone attacks on the West Coast, while noting it lacked details on timing, method, targets, or perpetrators. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/fbi-warned-california-that-iran-could-launch-drones-at-the-west-coast-report-trump-says-not-worried/article70732829.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>California officials: State officials said they had found no specific, credible threats and did not see an imminent drone-attack risk. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/11/world/middleeast/iran-california-drones-fbi.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-says-he-not-worried-about-iran-backed-attacks-us-soil'>Trump says he is not worried about Iran-backed attacks on US soil</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/fbi-warned-california-that-iran-could-launch-drones-at-the-west-coast-report-trump-says-not-worried/article70732829.ece'>FBI warned California that Iran could launch drones at the West Coast: report; Trump says ‘not worried’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/11/world/middleeast/iran-california-drones-fbi.html'>California Officials See No Imminent Threat of Drone Attacks by Iran</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/fbi-warns-iran-could-launch-drone-attack-on-california-as-conflict-in-west-asia-escalates-13988549.html'>FBI warns Iran could launch drone attack on California as conflict in West Asia escalates</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1rr1f4k/fbi_warns_iran_aspired_to_attack_california_with/'>FBI warns Iran aspired to attack Cali